       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="CTET Scorecard Download Link">
             <div class="blog-content">
                <div class="blog-body">
                    <h1 class="blog-title mb-4">Your Comprehensive Guide to Downloading the CTET Scorecard &amp; Certificate 2026</h1>
                    <p class="mb-4">The Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) is a crucial examination for aspiring teachers in India, qualifying them for teaching positions in central government schools and other institutions. Once you've appeared for the exam, accessing your scorecard and certificate is the next vital step. This guide will walk you through the entire process of downloading your CTET result, understanding the qualifying marks, and retrieving your valuable CTET certificate and marksheet from DigiLocker.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Latest CTET Exam Status: February 2026 Session</h2>
                    <p>The CTET February 2026 examination was successfully conducted on February 7th and 8th, 2026. Candidates are eagerly awaiting the release of the answer key, which is expected soon. Following the answer key release and the objection process, the CTET result for the February 2026 session is anticipated to be declared in March 2026, with some sources suggesting it could be released by the last week of February 2026. Keep an eye on the official CTET website for the most up-to-date announcements.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">How to Download Your CTET Scorecard from ctet.nic.in</h2>
                    <p>The CTET scorecard, displaying your marks and qualifying status, is initially released on the official CTET website. Follow these simple steps to download it:</p>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official Website</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Navigate to the official Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) website: <a href="https://ctet.nic.in" target="_blank">ctet.nic.in</a>.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Result Link</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for the link that says "CTET February 2026 Result" or similar, usually found in the 'Latest News' section.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Your Roll Number</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Click on the result link. You will be redirected to a new login window where you need to enter your CTET roll number.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">4. View and Download Your Scorecard</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">After entering your roll number, click on the 'Submit' button. Your CTET scorecard for both Paper 1 and Paper 2 (if applicable) will be displayed on the screen. Download and print it for your records and future reference.</div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Understanding CTET Qualifying Marks</h2>
                    <p>To qualify for the CTET exam, candidates must achieve a minimum percentage of marks as set by the Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) and the National Council for Teacher Education (NCTE). These criteria are consistent for both Paper 1 and Paper 2.</p>

                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ General Category: Candidates must score 60% or above to be declared qualified.</p>
                        <p>✅ Reserved Categories (OBC/SC/ST/PwD): Candidates need to score a minimum of 55% to qualify.</p>
                    </div>

                    <p class="mt-4">Here's a detailed breakdown of the passing marks:</p>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Category</th>
                                <th>Minimum Percentage</th>
                                <th>Minimum Marks (Out of 150)</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td>General</td>
                                <td>60%</td>
                                <td>90 Marks</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>OBC/SC/ST/PwD</td>
                                <td>55%</td>
                                <td>82 Marks</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                    <p>School managements, including government, government-aided, and unaided schools, may offer concessions to reserved categories in accordance with their reservation policies.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Accessing Your CTET Certificate and Marksheet via DigiLocker</h2>
                    <p>The CBSE issues CTET mark sheets and eligibility certificates in digital format through the DigiLocker platform. These documents are digitally signed and are valid for a lifetime.</p>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Download or Visit DigiLocker</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Download the DigiLocker app on your mobile device (Android or iOS) or visit the official website: <a href="https://digilocker.gov.in" target="_blank">digilocker.gov.in</a>.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Log In to Your Account</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Log in using your registered mobile number or Aadhaar number. CBSE typically sends DigiLocker login credentials via SMS to candidates' registered mobile numbers. If you haven't received them, you can still log in using your Aadhaar.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">3. Navigate to 'Issued Documents'</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Once logged in, click on the 'Issued Documents' tab or 'Get More Now' on the homepage.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">4. Select CBSE Documents</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Search for and select 'Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE), Delhi' from the list of issuers.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">5. Choose CTET Marksheet/Certificate</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Click on 'Teacher Eligibility Test Marksheet/Certificate'.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">6. Enter Details and Download</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Enter your roll number and the year of passing the CTET exam. Check the box (if prompted) and click the download button. Your CTET certificate and marksheet will be available in PDF format.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="highlight-text">
                        <p><strong>Important Note:</strong> While all candidates who appeared for the exam can download their marksheet, only those who qualify with the minimum required marks will receive the CTET certificate.</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Key Details on Your CTET Scorecard</h2>
                    <p>Your CTET scorecard is more than just a pass/fail statement; it contains essential information about your performance:</p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ Candidate's Name and Roll Number</p>
                        <p>✅ Father's and Mother's Name</p>
                        <p>✅ Category (General, OBC, SC, ST, PwD)</p>
                        <p>✅ Subject-wise Marks Secured</p>
                        <p>✅ Total Score in CTET</p>
                        <p>✅ Exam Qualifying Status (Qualified/Not Qualified)</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)</h2>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">Q1. Is the CTET certificate valid for a lifetime?</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Yes, as per recent CBSE guidelines, the CTET certificate now holds lifetime validity for all categories.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">Q2. What if I don't receive DigiLocker credentials via SMS?</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">You can still log in to DigiLocker using your Aadhaar number or registered mobile number. The Aadhaar number acts as an authentication medium for CBSE.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">Q3. Can I challenge the CTET result?</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">No, the CTET result, once declared, is considered the final decision of the exam conducting authority. However, you can raise objections against the provisional answer key before the final result is declared.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">Q4. What is the process for obtaining a duplicate CTET marksheet or certificate?</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">You can obtain duplicate documents by visiting the official CTET website (ctet.nic.in), navigating to the 'Duplicate Marksheet &amp; Certificate' link under 'e-Services', and following the instructions. There might be a fee for this service (e.g., Rs. 500 for a duplicate certificate).</div>
                    </div>

                    <p class="mt-4">Downloading your CTET scorecard and certificate is a straightforward process once you know the steps. The CTET qualification opens up numerous opportunities in the teaching sector across India, making this certificate a valuable asset for your career. Good luck to all candidates!</p>
                </div>
            </div>
       </div>

            
            
